  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/FileParsers/MolSGroupParsing.cpp",
    "description": "The bug is a type-confusion/null-deref path caused by accepting malformed SGroup vector records (M  SAL / M  SBL / M  SPA) and passing parsed indices directly into SubstanceGroup bookmark-based adders. In ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine(), parsed integers are treated as bookmarks and dispatched to SubstanceGroup::addAtomWithBookmark()/addBondWithBookmark()/addParentAtomWithBookmark(). For this PoV, a corrupted SAL line leads to addAtomWithBookmark() being called with an invalid bookmark; dp_mol->getUniqueAtomWithBookmark() returns an invalid pointer state, and atom->getIdx() at SubstanceGroup.cpp:63 triggers UBSan dynamic-type crash (__dynamic_cast). Root cause is insufficient validation/sanitization of SGroup vector data before invoking bookmark lookups.",
    "conditions": "Data flow: mol_data_stream_to_mol_fuzzer -> MolDataStreamToMol() -> ParseMolBlockProperties() -> ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine() on an M  SAL/SBL/SPA line from attacker-controlled mol block text. Trigger requires malformed SGroup property lines that define/retain an SGroup entry and include invalid bookmark integers (e.g., huge/out-of-range/corrupted values) so the parser still reaches (sgroup->*sGroupAddIndexedElement)(nbr). In non-strict parsing this can proceed far enough to call addAtomWithBookmark() with bad bookmark data, causing crash when dereferencing the returned atom."
  },
